    "created_at": "2023-04-25T16:26:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-04-25T16:26:03Z",
    "body": "@nt1m if I'm reading https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/pull/11155 correctly, you implemented this behavior in `FullscreenManager.cpp`, but I'm unsure if all of the `isInPopoverShowingState()` checks are intended to always pass, or if there are also cases where a fullscreen request will be rejected because of an open popover?\r\n\r\nIf that PR matches this spec, can we consider that support from WebKit to make this change? I'd like to get it merged because it makes https://github.com/whatwg/fullscreen/pull/223 easier to understand, in particular it guarantees (in the spec) that certain combinations of fullscreen and popovers can't happen.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
